   <standOff><listPerson><person xml:id="person3756"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">asaṅga</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon thogs med</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">thogs myed</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6117</idno><idno type="APIS">3756</idno></person><person xml:id="person3786"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog blo ldan shes rab</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྔོག་བློ་ལྡན་ཤེས་རབ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog lo tsA ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo chen</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge slong blo ldan shes rab</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog lo rtsa ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog dge slong blo ldan shes rab</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">blo ldan bzang po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo tsha ba chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo ts+tsha ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo tsha ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lo tsa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rngog</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">blo ldan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ma hA</persName><birth notBefore="1059-01-01" notAfter="1059-12-31">1059</birth><death notBefore="1109-01-01" notAfter="1109-12-31">1109</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2551</idno><idno type="APIS">3786</idno><note type="comment">See [BAQ9MH4T]: 193 for the main events of his life.&#13;
&#13;
Three manuscript editions of his writings and translations were deposited respectively in rNgog Blo ldan shes rab's tomb, in the monastery of gSang phu (probably in the main assembly hall), and in Drin las kyi sde (ID:4357) ([7FZ3B926]: 107).</note></person><person xml:id="person3831"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phywa pa chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཕྱྭ་པ་ཆོས་ཀྱི་སེང་གེ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phya pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phya</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">cha pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi seng+ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">phya pa chos seng ge ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge' slong chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge bshes cha pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge bshes chen po phya pa chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon phya pa chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon cha pa chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon cha pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpal phya pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs pa'i dbang phyug phya pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs pa'i dbang phyug chos kyi seng ge</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhas pa chen po cha pa</persName><birth notBefore="1109-01-01" notAfter="1109-12-31">1109</birth><death notBefore="1169-04-23" notAfter="1169-04-23">1169-04-23</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1404</idno><idno type="APIS">3831</idno><note type="comment">The majority of the information available on Phya pa has been provided in [EZ5JXHJY] and [8S7FDMCJ]. Summaries of the same are also found in [LQZU66YX]: 37-40, [F4UK2S8P]: 2-3, and [BW9UR427]: 35-36 (in French).&#13;
&#13;
&#13;
On his birth in 1109, the year of rNgog Blo ldan shes rab (ID:3786)'s passing, see [TM8DW8WA]: 32-33, [VKBZTBWN]: 4b4-5, and [8GL7ZT7Y]: 15b2-3.&#13;
On the date of his passing in a "sa mo glang" year, see [R894SIKE]: 400, [VKBZTBWN]: 4b4-5 and 6a5. &#13;
[95UZA9Y5]: 40/3/5 (reported in [7FZ3B926]: 111 and [MPRU5QUC]: 206) specifies the day "sa mo glang gi lo'i nag pa zla ba nag po'i phyogs kyi tshes brgyad," i.e., on the 23rd of the third month.&#13;
&#13;
A list of his students is provided in [EZ5JXHJY]: 356, based on [MQB8JGAX]: 297/4, [KL9XTQWI]: I, 454, [4YEPFBIB]: 340-341, [8GL7ZT7Y], fol. 15b3, [VKBZTBWN], fol. 4b7-5a4.&#13;
[FDEWZ2NZ]: 290 also mentions the list of the four "jo sras" from bSod nams dpal's Bla ma rngog pa yab sras rim par byon pa’i rnam thar rin po che’i rgyan gyi phreng ba.&#13;
&#13;
'Gos lo tsa ba lists numerous works composed before Phya pa took the see of gSang phu; these include commentaries and summaries on the Five works of Maitreya, the Pramāṇaviniścaya, the Satyadvayavibhaṅga, Madhyamakālaṃkāra, Madhyamakāloka, and  Bodhicaryāvatāra. He mentions having seen these, the Yid kyi mun sel (ID:4503) and summaries on Madhyamaka, as well as (ID:4505) and (ID:5971). See exX0032026-04-2304-02-58 .&#13;
'Gos lo tsa ba does not mention any composition dealing with monastic discipline. &#13;
&#13;
Śākya mchog ldan ([TM8DW8WA], 12-13 and 32) mentions a (doubtful) commentary on the Pramāṇavārttika (ID:3772) in addition to the commentary on the Pramāṇaviniścaya, and three summaries (small, intermediate, large), the intermediate one being the Yid kyi mun sel (ID:4503). (Discussed in [EZ5JXHJY]: 357, translated in [8S7FDMCJ]: 59).&#13;
&#13;
Four groups of students are mentioned in Tibetan sources (which do not imply that the members of the respective groups were studying with Phya pa at the same time), with occasional variations:&#13;
&#13;
1) The "Eight Great Lions" (seng chen brgyad). Eight scholars whose names contains the expression "seng ge," likely connoting their expertise in epistemology. The standard list includes gTsang nag pa (ID:3839), Dan 'bag (ID:3840), 'Bru sha (ID:3841), rMa bya (ID:3842), rTsags/rTsegs (ID:4289), Myang/Nyang bran (ID:3844), and gNyal pa/dMyal ma (ID:6679). The eighth one is instead sometimes said to be gTsang pa 'Jam dpal (ID:6336), 'U yug pa (ID:3846), or mTshur ston (DI:4315).&#13;
&#13;
2) The "four sons of noble families" (jo sras mi bzhi) or the "three sons of noble families" (jo sras gsum). They are young noble men of the rNgog (ID:3847), 'Khon (ID:3848), Khu (ID:3849), and gNyos/sMyos (ID:3850). The four are listed in [VKBZTBWN]: 4a7 and [8GL7ZT7Y]: 15b3, whereas on 16a1 the author speaks of "jo sras gsum." The four are also listed by bSod nams dpal, see [FDEWZ2NZ]: 290.&#13;
&#13;
3) The "three wise ones" (shes rab can mi gsum) or "four wise ones" (shes rab can mi bzhi). The threefold-list in [VKBZTBWN]: 5a1 has rKong po (ID:3852), lHo pa sgom gzan (ID:3853), Par bu ba/sPar phu ba (ID:3854). 'Gar dbang grub (ID:3851) is added in the fourfold list, e.g. in [R894SIKE]: 406.&#13;
&#13;
4) The "three accomplished ones" (grub thob mi gsum). These are students who later became famous masters: Dus gsum mkhyen pa (ID:3855), Phag mo gru pa (ID:3856), gSal sto (ID:3857). The third is sometimes replaced by Zhang tshal (ID:6409), or is suggested to be the latter's direct student.</note></person><person xml:id="person3834"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgya dmar ba byang chub grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྒྱ་དམར་བ་བྱང་ཆུབ་གྲགས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">stod lung rgya dmar ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">stod lungs rgya dmar pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dam pa stod lung pa rgya dmar ba</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">stod rgya</persName><birth notBefore="1054-01-01" notAfter="1075-12-31">after 1054 before 1075</birth><death notBefore="1135-01-01" notAfter="1194-12-31">after 1135 before 1194</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P4749</idno><idno type="APIS">3834</idno><note type="comment">Floruit 1095–1135. [YF8Z2ZGH]: 332 "rGya dmar pa was not only fully learned, but also possessed numerous Tantric secret precepts."</note></person><person xml:id="person3864"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jad pa byang chub skyabs</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འཇད་པ་བྱང་ཆུབ་སྐྱབས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jad pa slob dpon ston skyabs</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jad pa ston skyabs</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jad pa byang skyabs</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhas pa byang chub skyabs</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang skyabs</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub skyabs</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">skyabs</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jad</persName><birth notBefore="1100-01-01" notAfter="1157-12-31">after 1100 before 1157</birth><death notBefore="1177-01-01" notAfter="1237-12-31">after 1177 before 1237</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P3779</idno><idno type="APIS">3864</idno></person><person xml:id="person3876"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">nyang bran pa chos kyi ye shes</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཉང་བྲན་པ་ཆོས་ཀྱི་ཡེ་ཤེས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ye shes</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi ye shes</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">myang bran pa chos ye</persName><birth notBefore="1060-01-01" notAfter="1130-12-31">after 1060 before 1130</birth><death notBefore="1150-01-01" notAfter="1210-12-31">after 1150 before 1210</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P4458</idno><idno type="APIS">3876</idno><note type="comment">Maybe the same person as "Nyang bran chos kyi seng ge" (ID:3844), as suggested in [CCSBSVCA]: 164, n. 416.  However, A khu ching distinguishes the two.&#13;
Author of manuals on the Śīkṣāsamuccaya (ID:3742) - see (ID: 6558) - and Bodhicaryāvatāra (ID: 3727). See [R894SIKE]: 405 (zhang tshe spong ba chos kyi bla mas kyang TI ka 'ga' re brtsams shing de'i slob ma nyan bran pa chos kyi ye shes kyis ni bslabs pa kun las btus pa dang | byang chub sems dpa'i spyod pa la 'jug pa la sogs pa spyod phyogs kyi yig cha dang |) and [EG6VZ8JK]: 26, translated from [8GL7ZT7Y]: 15b2 (chos kyi ye shes kyis bslab spyod sogs byang chub sems dpa’i sde sogs la bshad nyan yun ring zhing rnam bshad mang po mdzad ).</note></person><person xml:id="person4012"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'gar dharma smon lam</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འགར་དྷརྨ་སྨོན་ལམ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dar ma smon lam</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dhar ma smon lam</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dha rma smon lam</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">d+har+ma smon lam</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'gar chos smon</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'gar chos kyi smon lam</persName><birth notBefore="1100-01-01">after 1100</birth><death notAfter="1250-12-31">before 1250</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P3JT13455</idno><idno type="APIS">4012</idno></person><person xml:id="person4013"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dol rgya bsod nams byang chub</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">དོལ་རྒྱ་བསོད་ནམས་བྱང་ཆུབ</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4013</idno></person><person xml:id="person4014"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">zhang bye ma lha khang pa bsod nams ye shes</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཞང་བྱེ་མ་ལྷ་ཁང་པ་བསོད་ནམས་ཡེ་ཤེས</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4014</idno></person><person xml:id="person4253"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">myang chen po</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">མྱང་ཆེན་པོ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">smon lam</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">4253</idno></person><person xml:id="person4291"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ngur smrig pa dar ma snying po</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ངུར་སྨྲིག་པ་དར་མ་སྙིང་པོ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ngur mig pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dar ma snying po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ngur smrig pa chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ngur dmigs pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rong gi dge bshes ngur dmig pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brang ti dar ma snying po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brang ti dar snying</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'brang</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ngur mig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'ur smrig</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">brang ti</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rdu</persName><birth notAfter="1085-12-31">before 1085</birth><death notBefore="1105-01-01">after 1105</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P10011</idno><idno type="APIS">4291</idno><note type="comment">We follow Stearns ([RA3FK3BK]: 245, n. 173 and n. 176) in assuming that Ngur smrig pa is the same person as Brang ti Dar ma snying po, a foremost figure in the transmission of the Abhidharma in Tibet.&#13;
